{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1305392-dividing-a-thing-from-itself-cleaving-things-with-correspondence","id":1305392,"title":"Dividing a Thing from Itself (cleaving things with Correspondence)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-16T20:52:05-07:00","id":1305392,"title":"Dividing a Thing from Itself (cleaving things with Correspondence)","content":"If I remember right, you need conjunctional Life to, say, teleport someone's spleen with Correspondence. I'm of the mind that Effects should be decoupled as much as possible, and more things should be possible without conjunction than are suggested in the book. But there does seem to be a good metaphysical reason why dividing solid objects or creatures with Correspondence should at least be <i>hard</i>. Correspondence ranges are based on closeness of association. Things that are physically part of other things are especially, perhaps uniquely close. But to satisfy game metaphysics and game balance, all you have to do is raise the success threshold for dividing things with Correspondence--unless the mage also has Life 2 [Edit: or Matter if the object is not living].","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","user":"Faradn","date":". 04-16-2019, 11:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T22:19:39-07:00","id":1305405,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'm quite fine with requiring conjunctional spheres being required for teleporting somebody organ's out, really.<br /> Granted, simply requiring a lot more sucesses instead would be an interesting houserule, but in my mind, affecting parts of a single pattern is a good reason for the conjunctional rule (as is locking). But, as I said, it would make for a fine houserule.<br /> <br /> <br /> ...that said this reminds me of a Wonder I came up with once;<br /> <br /> Consider a long blade that does not harm you. It does not even *hurt* you. Instead, when it passes through a matter or life pattern, it separates that pattern along its cutting line with a correspondence tunnel <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> That is, you slice through somebody's arm, and the arm...simply falls off. It's still alive. The cut is almost cartoonish in the way that nothing, ahem, comes out of the cuts since the two pieces are actually still connected, but separated by space. The arm can still move, the target can still feel it, but it's laying on the floor next to them.<br /> The neat thing is that such a quirky non-lethal weapon would be incredibly effective - it would ignore armor, it would ignore soak, heck it would ignore any material resistance or structure as it does not really damage anything physically at all. Depending on where it cuts, it simply hinders the target through physical misplacement and confusing the hell out of the senses.<br /> <br /> And as soon as you end the wonder effect, everything snaps back as it should be. Quite a gentle (if macabre) nonlethal weapon. And/or door opener.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Using standard rules, this Wonder would require Correspondence 4, Life 4, Matter 2 for its effect. A more potent version would include Forces 2 as well - not even a kinetic shield would protect the target. Everything shall be gently separated.<br /> Note: While the mandatory inclusion of Matter 2 - you want to make it go through stuff like clothes after all - also means it could be used against vamps, making it effective against shifters would also require Spirit 2.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, with your houserule all of this would be doable with Correspondence alone - the question is how much you'd want to boost the threshold, depending on all the things it's supposed to handle. It could grow quite high. Would the threshold rise depending on the amount of other spheres that'd be normally involved? On level of highest sphere? A combination?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 04-17-2019, 03:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T23:36:28-07:00","id":1305412,"title":"","content":"By the way, Faradn, regarding your houserule...another option would be to limit pure-correspondence separations to non-lethal applications <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> That way Correspondence gains a lot of single-sphere utility, but in order to do actual Damage you'd have to use the standard conjunctional rules.<br /> <br /> Also, it's worth remembering that the standard conjunctional rule does something else in regards to Correspondence: It makes you need higher levels of it, depending on the target pattern. It's best to keep that in place, else Correspondence 2 becomes *very* powerful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 04-17-2019, 03:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T00:52:25-07:00","id":1305415,"title":"","content":"Something you could do that wouldn't muck too much with the metaphysics and balance issues?<br /> <br /> Teleporting out just pieces with Correspondence colocates them, not divides them. So you can use Correspondence (and a small bit of the relevant Pattern Spheres) to hold someone's spleen in your hand... but it's still operating completely normally as if it was still in the body. So if you summon up a car's gas tank, the car will run just fine, and as it does gas will flow from the tank across space, into the engine as normal. But you could sabotage it yourself after doing so, and then send it back or whatever.<br /> <br /> It's not really any more powerful than using Correspondence to do long range effects in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T02:45:21-07:00","id":1305422,"title":"","content":"Yeah I'm glad that Correspondence can't actually divide a pattern. You can teleport a cat into your arms, but you can't teleport someone's head into your hands, since their head is attached to their body (the Life pattern) and dividing it would demand the use of the Life Sphere and enough successes to do the lethal damage necessary to separate a head from a body.<br /> <br /> So now we're looking at a vulgar Life 3 (?) effect, so Correspondence 3 as well, and that means difficulty 7, and you'll need enough successes to bridge the gap between the head and you (let's say 1, for in sight) and enough successes with Life to do 7 points of damage (that's 4 successes, assuming the target can't soak the Lethal damage, and doesn't have any bonus health levels; a cyborg might end up with a dislocated joint in their neck and some damaged bones instead of decapitation).<br /> <br /> So 5 successes at a base difficulty of 7 or 8 seems somewhat reasonable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}